      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): bound app-server websocket handshake waits at 30s",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators using Codex app-server over `websocket`/`unix` transport would hang forever on `initialize`/RPC when a peer accepted TCP but never completed the WebSocket upgrade. Pending frames never flush and the client never sees a transport exit, so the run cannot fail closed or reconnect.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Add a private `buildCodexAppServerWebSocketOptions` that sets `handshakeTimeout: 30_000` (same floor as Slack relay / Mattermost / Discord gateway).\n- Both TCP and Unix upgrade paths consume that builder.\n- Guard `EventEmitter` error re-emit with `listenerCount` so callers that only wait on `exit` (handshake hang paths) are not disrupted by Node's unhandled-`error` throw.\n- Regressions observe production wiring in source (knip-safe) and prove stalled-handshake exit + `initialize` failure with a short test-only hang floor.\n\nNo new config/env surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** A Codex app-server endpoint that accepted TCP without completing the websocket handshake could pin `initialize`/RPC forever on that attempt.\n\n**After:** Handshake waits fail closed after 30s (`Opening handshake has timed out` → transport `exit` / client error), so the run can stop or recover instead of hanging.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCompete check (live, before push): no open PR for `createWebSocketTransport` / Codex app-server `handshakeTimeout` (siblings Mattermost `#105553`, Signal `#106471`, ClickClack `#106485`, QQBot `#106484` are different owners).\n\nLocal proof:\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/transport-websocket.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n✓ can speak JSON-RPC over websocket transport\n✓ can speak JSON-RPC over the canonical unix control socket\n✓ uses a 30s handshakeTimeout matching Slack relay / Mattermost\n[codex handshake proof] timed_out=true elapsed_ms=200 code=1006 handshakeTimeout_ms=200 production_ms=30000\n✓ emits exit when the websocket handshake never completes\n[codex handshake initialize proof] timed_out=true elapsed_ms=202 message=initialize transport failed after request write: Opening handshake has timed out\n✓ fails initialize when the websocket handshake never completes\n\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  5 passed (5)\n```\n\nNegative control (same TCP-accept / never-upgrade fixture): without `handshakeTimeout`, `ws` stays `CONNECTING` and never emits `exit` (standalone repro before the fix). With the short test floor, exit arrives in ~200ms; production wiring asserts the 30s constant.\n\nAutoreview: Codex engine invocation failed in this environment (engine JSON schema dump / no actionable findings returned); manual review of owner path + sibling Mattermost/Signal handshake PRs found no remaining blockers for this narrow fix.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
        "branch": "fix/codex-app-server-ws-handshake-timeout",
